<p>Hi {{{Recovery__c.Contact_First_Name__c}}},</p>

<p>We wanted to let you know that we are unable to process your reimbursement claim using the bank details you provided. You'll need to check your bank details and re-submit using our secure portal.</p>

<h3>How to organise your reimbursement</h3>

<p>To process your reimbursement, you will need to provide us with your bank account details using our secure case portal. If you’re unsure about your bank details, you’ll need to check with your bank before re-submission. Visit <a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/customer-care-feedback-form/update-customer-care-case.html</a> to update your details.<br />
<br />
All customers will receive email notifications about the progress of the claim. If you are a Qantas Frequent Flyer member, you can conveniently track your reimbursement via the request tracker in the Qantas app via ‘Track my cases’ in Help and Support.</p>

<h3>Need help?</h3>

<p>Call us on 13 13 13 (in Australia) or your local&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us.html">Qantas Office</a>&nbsp;for assistance.</p>

<p>Have your Customer care reference number {{{Recovery__c.Parent_Case__c}}} ready to enter.</p>

<h3>If you’re suspicious</h3>

<p>Not sure something is genuine? Remember, Qantas will never ask you to&nbsp;<u>email</u>&nbsp;your bank account details,&nbsp;credit card, PIN, or passwords.<br />
For more advice and warnings on scams please visit the Qantas scam assistance page -&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html" rel="noreferrer noopener" target="_blank">https://www.qantas.com/au/en/support/contact-us/scam-assistance.html</a></p>
